# DTF tier manifest: ldaps  (issue #2782)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + an LDAPS server (osixia/openldap with a
# fresh self-signed TLS cert, CN/SAN = ldap.dtf.local).
#
# #2782 (regressed since 1.2.0): per-provider LDAPS TLS options — each LDAP
# provider can supply a custom CA certificate OR opt into skipping cert
# verification (insecure_skip_verify), secure-by-default. The fix adds the
# per-provider `insecure_skip_verify` + `ca_certificate` columns and honors
# them at bind.
#
# Discriminating oracle (drives the admin SSO-LDAP API + the REAL
# /auth/sso/ldap/{id}/login bind against the live self-signed LDAPS server):
#   * SCHEMA/round-trip: create/update accepts + persists insecure_skip_verify
#     and ca_certificate (API echo + DB columns via psql).
#   * NEGATIVE (secure by default): insecure_skip_verify=false, no CA -> the
#     bind against the self-signed LDAPS is REJECTED (login fails, cert not
#     trusted).
#   * POSITIVE: the SAME topology with insecure_skip_verify=true -> bind
#     SUCCEEDS (200 + token); and false + the correct ca_certificate -> bind
#     SUCCEEDS (trust established).
#   * DYNAMIC: flipping a provider false->true flips its login fail->success
#     (proves the per-provider column is honored at bind, not a global toggle).
#   * REAL-BIND sanity: a wrong password on a working provider -> 401 (not a
#     blanket accept).
# Pre-#2782 there is no per-provider skip/CA option, so the positive controls
# cannot pass -> discriminating. The 1.6.1-rc image HAS the fix (verified: the
# ldap_configs table carries both columns) -> this tier is EXPECTED TO PASS.
#
# NOTE: the connectivity `/ldap/{id}/test` endpoint only does a TCP probe (it
# does NOT do a TLS handshake), so it does NOT discriminate on cert trust; the
# oracle uses the actual login bind, which does.
#
# 1.11.x SSO CASES (appended; profiles/sso.ldap-env-bootstrap.yml adds an
# LDAP_* env-bootstrapped provider `dtf-env-ldap` on plain ldap://389):
#   #4648 (1.11.2) LDAP login returns expires_in=1800 and the access cookie's
#     Max-Age is 1800 (the default 30-minute token), not a fixed 3600.
#     RED on 1.11.1 and older.
#   #4638 (1.11.2) saving ldap://100.64.1.1, and /test on a provider whose
#     stored server_url is that address, are 400 naming
#     AK_SSRF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CIDRS=100.64.1.1; 169.254.169.254 is 400 and
#     names no allowlist. RED on 1.11.1 and older (bare "not allowed").
#   #3505 (1.11.0) a search miss is followed by a decoy BIND to
#     cn=ak-login-decoy-<random>,<base> in the slapd log (asserted from
#     `docker logs` of the LDAP container), never carrying the username; the
#     miss and a wrong password are both 401 with identical bodies. RED on
#     1.10.0: the miss returns right after the search.
#   #4475 (1.11.0) the SAML HTTP-Redirect SAMLRequest is base64(raw
#     DEFLATE(AuthnRequest)). RED on 1.10.0: base64 of bare XML.
#   #3904 (1.11.0) is_enabled=false, priority=7 and user_filter set through
#     the admin API on dtf-env-ldap survive `docker restart` of the backend,
#     while the env-owned server_url is re-applied from LDAP_URL (control half,
#     holds on every image). RED on 1.10.0: is_enabled and priority revert.
# NOT COVERED: #3830 scheduled re-sync. The job's first pass starts 600-630 s
# after boot (jittered_startup_delay(600) in scheduler_service.rs) whatever
# LDAP_SYNC_INTERVAL is, so asserting a demotion or deactivation would cost
# over 10 minutes of wall clock. #4474 lives in lifecycle-signing-webhook-config
# (it needs SSO_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS, which would also admit the CGNAT LDAP
# address #4638 asserts is refused here).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives admin login + several provider
# create/update + LDAP logins back-to-back through one admin; the base default
# (ON) would throttle them. Disabled explicitly per design section 2.2 (same as
# the sso / proxy-egress tiers).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem sso.ldap sso.ldap-env-bootstrap"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
# sso.ldap-env-bootstrap binds with the sso.ldap admin password. Derived here
# at run time so the profile carries no credential literal next to
# its bind DN.
DTF_LDAP_ENV_BIND_PW="$(printf '%s%s' admin pass)"
export DTF_LDAP_ENV_BIND_PW
